d endpoints and budgets</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C15"><data key="title">Permutation symmetry is about complete input relabelings</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C16"><data key="title">Coevolution changes what is being evaluated</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C17"><data key="title">Champion selection changes the mathematical question</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C18"><data key="title">The 2005 biological limitation has stated boundaries</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C19"><data key="title">An oracle formalizes an observation interface</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C20"><data key="title">Full-row simulation preserves equal-call dominance</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C21"><data key="title">Active information is relative to a baseline</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C22"><data key="title">The weak search-for-search bound needs a mean premise</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C23"><data key="title">The strict simplex tail uses a stronger measure</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C24"><data key="title">Physics can induce a structured problem distribution</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C25"><data key="title">A mechanism measure need not have simplex tails</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C26"><data key="title">Fixed targets differ from environmental alignment</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C27"><data key="title">Elementary costs can reverse oracle comparisons</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C28"><data key="title">Finite populations can track persistent environments</data><data key="node_type">claim</data></node><node id="C29"><data key="title">A success statistic does not identify causal provenance</data><data key="